nformatika\n   DOI: https://doi.org/10.37373/tekno.v14i1.2526\n   Why it matters: Discusses a retrieval-augmented generation chatbot specifically designed for academic information services, indicating a practical evaluation.\n\n3. Title: \"Digital and social media marketing: a bibliometric mapping from 2020 to 2025\"\n   Publication date: 2026-11-12\n   First author: Yaser A. Alwasly\n   Venue: Future Business Journal\n   DOI: https://doi.org/10.1186/s43093-026-01036-9\n   Why it matters: Provides bibliometric mapping of digital and social media marketing which may include insights into retrieval-augmented generation applications.\n\n4. Title: \"HEAL-RAG: A Hybrid Evolving Retrieval-Augmented Generation Framework for Explainable Biomedical Data Analysis and Clinical Decision Support\"\n   Publication date: 2026-11-12\n   First author: Ronke Seyi Babatunde\n   Venue: Algorithms\n   DOI: https://doi.org/10.3390/a19110992\n   Why it matters: Introduces a hybrid retrieval-augmented generation framework targeting explainability and clinical decision support in biomedical data analysis.\n\n5. Title: \"Evaluating Embedding Models and Preprocessing for Retrieval of MDE Elements in RAG Systems\"\n   Publication date: 2026-11-12\n   First author: Julian Roßkothen\n   Venue: KITopen\n   DOI: https://doi.org/10.5445/ir/1000196452/pub\n   Why it matters: Focuses on evaluation of embedding models and preprocessing techniques critical to retrieval in retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) systems.\n\n6. Title: \"An Explainable Semantic Enterprise Research Network for Institutional Collaboration Recommendation\"\n   Publication date: 2026-11-12\n   First author: Ameen Shaheen\n   Venue: International Journal of Electronics and Communication Engineering\n   DOI: https://doi.org/10.14445/23488549/ijece-v13i10p114\n   Why it matters: Presents an explainable semantic enterprise network which may involve retrieval augmented generation methods for collaboration recommendation.\n\n7. Title: